## Configure the Agent

* Define clear AR-related topics (e.g., "Check My Balance," "Why Was My Claim Denied?").
* Set up two main flows: one for self-service resolution and one for escalation to finance/collections.
* Apply explicit guardrails to ensure the agent only answers within scope and triggers escalation when needed.

---

## Set Up Retrieval Logic

* Enable RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) to pull current claim and payment data.
* Create prompts for common AR scenarios to guide clients through self-service before escalation.
* Ensure logs and audit trails are kept for compliance.

---

## Prompt Builder

* Develop custom prompt templates focused on AR workflows (e.g., "Retrieve My Payment Status," "Explain My Denial Reason").
* Use knowledge snippets combined with live data retrieval to provide accurate, contextual responses.

---

## Design Actions (Optional)

* Use Flow automations to handle background processes like logging, case creation, and task routing to finance.
* Automatically create a support case if a question remains unresolved after self-service attempts.
* Record client actions and handoffs for reporting and future optimization.

